From ae8c88bc3776d3780fc1758abd76569e7964f209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hangxiang Ma <hangxiang.ma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:49:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 193/194] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: Describe disabled camera
 resources

Adapt the standalone-PHY layout from Hangxiang Ma's Kaanapali v24 series
using SM8750 register addresses, sizes and interrupts verified against the
saved runtime device tree. Add CAMSS, three CCI controllers, six CSI2 PHYs
and the SM8750 PHY clock OPPs. Keep all new controllers and CCI child buses
disabled; board supply, pinctrl and endpoint integration is separate.

The IFE-lite stock mapping includes a0x1000 CSID prefix. Map its0x1800 VFE
tail to match the candidate VFE980 offsets, with no overlapping resource
reservation. CCI explicitly requests the37.5 MHz clock used by the base
CCI v2 timing table. PHY rates match the SM8750 CAMCC frequency table.

Compiled DT checks compare all10 CAMSS resources,6 PHYs and3 CCI controllers
against stock FDT, including IOMMU stream and disabled state. The board DTB
build has only the existing hypervisor/DSI warnings. No hardware activation.

Based on: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261102-kaanapali-camss-v24-0-d6b8f3f6f66f@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: Hangxiang Ma <hangxiang.ma@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@localhost>
